From: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_sync: add hci_test_quirk compat helper for 6.12
Date: 2026-07-27

Armbian's drv-bluetooth-hci-sprd-broken-park-link-quirk-v6.1-6.15.patch
(added to sunxi-6.12 on 2026-07-27) calls hci_test_quirk(), a helper
that only exists since kernel 6.16 -- on 6.12 the build fails with
"implicit declaration of function 'hci_test_quirk'". Provide the 6.12
equivalent as a local static inline so the call compiles and behaves
identically (quirks are a bitmap in hdev->quirks on this kernel).
Harmless if Armbian fixes or drops their patch: an unused static
inline generates no warning.

Signed-off-by: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -19,6 +19,14 @@
 #include "aosp.h"
 #include "leds.h"

+/* Compat for out-of-tree patches written against >= 6.16, where
+ * hci_test_quirk() replaced open-coded test_bit() on hdev->quirks.
+ */
+static inline bool hci_test_quirk(const struct hci_dev *hdev, int quirk)
+{
+	return test_bit(quirk, &hdev->quirks);
+}
+
 static void hci_cmd_sync_complete(struct hci_dev *hdev, u8 result, u16 opcode,
 				  struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
--
2.43.0
